y notification blockers/layout/UNO/history/fields/live-style/serialization lifetime remain unverified; no whole-module promotion or registered IO change. Iteration48 restores complete selected native continuous/phantom tree policy: bound rule flags, parent continuous fallback and orphan defaults, protected continuous prefix validation/last-descendant traversal, public predecessor modes excluding the root, continuous suffix invalidation and upward cache/notification propagation. SwList validation follows NotifyInvalidChildren under actual document reading policy rather than eager hierarchical recursion; legacy callers resolve client document context. Continuous legacy numeric markers select the current level, while explicit ListFormat behavior and measured NONE guards remain unchanged.42 complete unchanged pinned native definitions produce960 sequences/69120 record states,5 policy profiles and64 full marker states under ASan/UBSan. Literal project tests compare real connected attributes,raw prefix caches,ordered reads,notifications,client lists and numbered registry through insertion,restart,count/reparent/removal/flag changes and reading transitions; source-body hashes and literal result integrity revalidated after deletion of source copies. Native bound start/type/raw format presence,pool,string/document-position/range/style,shown/no-layout/no-redline/dtor/fuzz/field/raw callback/broadcaster/static-service/decimal formatter aliases explicitly limit the proof;prior complete selected rule/format defaults remain separately supported. Actual Worker owners retain continuous/phantom flags and nested counters;copy/reset retain native scalar boundaries and supported genuine ODT level fields. No upstream code is invoked by project tests or persisted in task artifacts;manual probes generate only ignored scratch source. Full native layout/redline/original root arrays,live style/Font/graphics/other numeric families,service/global/destructor/name-map/GrabBag/UNO/full ODT metadata/UI lifetimes remain individually unverified. No whole-module,status,goal or registered IO/recovery/dependency/policy/coverage promotion. Iteration52 restores protected GetRoot access without changing its body or zero-argument nullable result. The existing browser SwList.GetListItem projection now checks the exact highest parent identity through native public GetParent links, without a public root surrogate, cast, text-node mapping or cache read. Six existing diagnostic files preserve177 matcher/expected-argument records while using test-only protected observers. New type/root/list tests cover protected base/subclass access, skipped phantoms through level9, root/orphan absence, owned/foreign/missing/different-document membership and explicit remove/re-add allocation plus list moves. Four fresh pinned file hashes and seven declaration/body hashes support manual source inspection only; no new compiled native range/redline/owner/destructor lifetime parity claim. Project tests never access upstream; no helper/native source bodies in task artifacts. Other child-container/count/access and wider lifetime obligations remain separately unverified; no status,whole-module,goal,registered IO/recovery or gate promotion. Iteration53 restores protected mChildren storage and native public zero-argument numeric GetChildCount, removes invented public GetChildren, and adapts SwList.HasNodes to the count. SwNodeNum scans protected children and retains the native dynamic type guard before Writer counting/recursive calls. Eight existing observer suites preserve249 matcher argument AST records through32 test-only protected storage observations. Three new tests cover exact visibility/arity/result, subclass storage, direct real/phantom/orphan counts through level9 removal and nonvalidating list membership, plus non-Writer child rejection. Five fresh pinned file hashes and six declaration/body hashes support manual inspection only; no new compiled native or full multi-root section/redline/lifetime claim. Existing policy method access and ordered-set container architecture remain separate measured obligations. No project test accesses upstream; no helper/native source bodies stored as task artifacts; no status/default/whole-module/goal or registered IO/recovery/gate promotion. Iteration63 restores mandatory operation document context across existing numbering tree mutations and notifications, SwList insert/remove/validate and SwNumRule.Validate, with protected Notify traversal. Text insertion/removal and node moves pass their owned document explicitly; first-client/text-derived operation fallbacks are removed while real-record reading policy retains text-owner precedence. Five owned tests and16 exact type/visibility checks cover empty/clientless roots, distinct owner/operation reading flags, rule invalidate-before-validate forwarding, actual insertion/removal, retained topology/raw caches and protected root/phantom traversal. Three new runtime cases and baseline type assertions fail before correction and pass afterward; old test matcher arguments are unchanged. Fresh pinned manual declaration/body/call-site hashes only; no native execution, helper/source artifacts or upstream access by project tests. Native text notification ownership/temporary blockers, dtor/client lifetimes, redline/range roots, complete access/const/final architecture, layout and browser obligations remain separately unverified. No whole-module/status/default/goal, registered IO/recovery or gate promotion.",
